Room: the host picks where a Room profile's download goes.

The host's downloads list chooses every download's file: the folder from
Room's Settings and Chrome's "name (1).ext" numbering (the Engine protocol's
willBeginDownload, Phase 2.6b), and Room carries no danger verdicts (Safe
Browsing is off in Chapter 3). Chrome decides the target in
DownloadTargetDeterminer (its own folder, a Save As panel when asked, Safe
Browsing and file-type verdicts).

No existing hook: the target decision is
DownloadManagerDelegate::DetermineDownloadTarget, and the delegate is
ChromeDownloadManagerDelegate, created and owned per profile by
DownloadCoreServiceImpl (its replacement setter is test-only); the
determiner's own delegate is the same object. //room answers only for new
downloads (no target yet) of profiles whose host set a downloads delegate;
resumed downloads, transient ones and every other profile keep Chrome's
determiner.

Phase 3.4a, 2026-10-05. //room: room/core/room_downloads.mm.
